// NOTE: DNS Hostname Support Added
// The connect_printer() method now supports both IP addresses and DNS hostnames.
// 
// Usage:
//   - IP address: "192.168.1.100" (existing behavior)
//   - Hostname: "printer.local" or "orca-printer.local" (new behavior)
//   - FQDN: "printer.example.com" (new behavior)
//
// The implementation automatically detects the input type and performs DNS resolution
// when necessary using the DNSResolver utility class.
//
// Example:
//   m_agent->connect_printer(dev_id, "orca-printer.local", "bblp", password, true);
//
// Files modified:
// - src/slic3r/Utils/NetworkAgent.hpp
// - src/slic3r/GUI/DeviceManager.cpp (MachineObject::connect method)
// - src/slic3r/Utils/DNSResolver.hpp/cpp (new files)
//
// The resolution is transparent to the caller - if a hostname is provided,
// it will be resolved to an IP address before being passed to the underlying
// printer communication layer.
